-- 367 — one market signal per taxonomy sector, each with its own evidence.
--
-- GENERATED FILE. Regenerate with:
--   python3 scripts/build-sector-signals.py --sql-out <this file>
--
-- WHY 79 OF 82 SECTOR PAGES SHOWED NO SIGNAL. The page asks
-- `GET /api/signals?sector=<taxonomy name>` and the worker matches that label
-- case-insensitively; the seeded feed only ever carried `Financial Services`,
-- `Technology` and `Healthcare`, so every other sector page said "No exact live
-- signal is recorded for this taxonomy label yet".
--
-- WHAT THE EVIDENCE IS. Every signal's evidence rows are real and attached:
-- Wikidata entity records for companies the sector's universe holds, plus live
-- Hacker News threads, public repositories and Stack Overflow questions pulled
-- from keyless public APIs, each with the URL a reader can open and the date it
-- was observed. The signal text was drafted from those inputs alone, under an
-- instruction not to state anything they do not contain: no market sizes, no
-- funding, no valuation, and no claim about a named company beyond its identity
-- facts. `confidence_score` and `freshness_score` use the same formulas the
-- worker's ranking engine recomputes at read time (`d_e`/`xB`).
--
-- TWO NEW SOURCE ROWS. `wikidata` and `company_website` are registered in
-- `signal_sources` rather than reporting Wikidata facts under
-- `registry_opencorporates`, which is a different register with a different
-- licence.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT. Signals upsert on their id and each signal's evidence is deleted
-- and rewritten, so a re-run cannot leave a signal with two generations of
-- evidence attached.

-- Sector signals + evidence, generated by scripts/build-sector-signals.py.
-- Idempotent per signal id; evidence rows are replaced for that signal.


